        <p>Cross Country Runnhig. The clubs of the Liverpool and District Cross Country Association, with one exception, took part in a huge harrier pack, on Saturday, for the opening of the cress-country season.- The weather was nnfavour- able, hut nevertheless 279 took part, and of this number 102 were novices. After a combined run of live miles, seniors and novices were Hoed up for mile " break " or races slow* the roads. Results.:— Seniors' Break : 1, J. Roberts, Sefton ; 2, C. J. Straw, Warrington ; 3, T. M. Walker, Liverpool G)mmasium ; 4, W. Clarke, Sefton ; 5, Birchall, North Liverpool Gymnasium ; 6, S. Welding, Sutton ; 7, W. (treenail, St. Helens ; 8, E. Waterson, Sefton and Liverpopl ; 0, J. H. Whittle, Farnworth.—Novices' Break : 1, C. Pye, Prescot Wireworks ;2, J. Garnett, St. Joseph's ; 3, L. Thompson, Prescot United.— Largest Musters : 1, Sacred Heart; St. Helens (11) ; 2, St. Helens, H. and A.C. (29) ;3, Liverpool Protes- tant Reformers (20).</p>
